                <head>192. Editorial Note</head>
                <p>On June 28, 1962, Adlai Stevenson sent President Kennedy a 6-page letter on
                    current disarmament problems. The letter is printed in full in <hi
                        rendition="#italic">The Papers of Adlai E. Stevenson: Ambassador to the
                        United Nations, 1961-1965</hi>, volume VIII, pages 265-269. Attached to a
                    copy of the letter in the Kennedy Library is a June 29 memorandum from Arthur
                    Schlesinger, Jr. to Carl Kaysen that reads, “You may wish to consider the
                    attached letter from Governor Stevenson—and also how best to answer it.”
                    (Kennedy Library, National Security Files, Kaysen Series, Disarmament, General,
                    6/61-12/62) No response to the letter has been found.</p>
            </div>
